                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "At this time, I can see there are a lot of negative reviews, but I must say I genuinely enjoyed this game.\n\nThe art, music and theming are all great—you play as a princess beating up yokai with a kendama, bow and arrows. The story is cute and simple, told mostly through cutscenes.\n\nConcerning gameplay, movements are indeed janky and combos are sluggish, but I learned you can animation-cancel by blocking during an attack, allowing you to defend yourself, move around, and chain combos a lot more easily. There are only four levels (and a bonus mode) and Hard mode is quite challenging, revolving around finesse, quick-thinking, and mastering each enemy and boss rather than simple button-mashing. That said, I would still only recommend this game to those who are willing to put mechanics second, and the overall vision first.",
